#: ../../source/docs/what-you-need.rst:5 460b939f2e4e48ddb60ac8da879ae378
msgid "What You Need to Build a MultiCopter"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/what-you-need.rst:7 f5f3536a1eee4d0886c044a1aedccbf0
msgid ""
"This article provides an overview of the main components you will need "
"when building a Copter-based multicopter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/what-you-need.rst:11 7597380684394f81ab62adca5705a151
msgid "Multicopter frame including motors, ESCs and propellers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/what-you-need.rst:13 46f547bef7ef4963accf1f3776c37665
msgid ""
"There are numerous frames, ESCs and motors available. Some components you"
" might consider are discussed in :ref:`Choosing a Multicopter Frame "
"<choosing-a-frame>` and the :ref:`Detailed Vehicle Builds <common-common-"
"airframe-builds>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/what-you-need.rst:18 4f9dea8b491642769d15835af7484dd3
msgid ""
"Many other designs and configurations including Traditional Helicopters "
"are also supported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/what-you-need.rst:22 faf3cdd562c248f08053b111c68ce5f6
msgid "6+ channel RC transmitter and receiver"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/what-you-need.rst:24 9d3f7c0a8bc54478b232229fa29e74db
msgid ""
"You'll need a radio control transmitter to manually control your Copter "
"and to activate its flight modes. You can use any RC transmitter/receiver"
" system with at least six channels. Some of the options are discussed in "
"the topic :ref:`Compatible RC Transmitter and Receiver Systems <common-"
"rc-systems>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/what-you-need.rst:33 90098dd6dd574523ae658f701deaa6fb
msgid "Autopilot (Autopilot hardware)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/what-you-need.rst:35 c34629eb50cd4d1ea6e3b60bcbec4558
msgid ""
"Copter's autopilot board determines its capabilities for autonomous "
"flight. See the :ref:`ArduPilot compatible autopilot page<common-"
"autopilots>` for a list. An autopilot with the following features is "
"recommended:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/what-you-need.rst:39 3ab3c811e5044ad093089e6f97d81f8c
msgid "An SD card for logging, terrain data base, scripting (if desired)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/what-you-need.rst:40 8e22fbf724b3427aae15eaab245d394e
msgid "Sufficient outputs for the number of motors and servos to be used"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/what-you-need.rst:41 e656623065f042d4b91782608ec87b3e
msgid "Sufficient number of UARTs for GPS, and telemetry radios, if desired"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/what-you-need.rst:42 64a9c0379f0e4544b61debe628768b21
msgid ""
"Vibration isolated IMU(s) is very desirable simplifying mounting "
"considerations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/what-you-need.rst:43 f749330cfcd24a9da6b5f906b43bcdab
msgid "Be sure the autopilot includes a barometer"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/what-you-need.rst:44 3a138408cbe14161a5190762d60024e8
msgid "I2C for external compass"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/what-you-need.rst:46 278e16d0d951426d9924587d8328e304
msgid ""
"many autopilots have an internal compass, but in order to avoid motor "
"interference, an external compass is sometimes desirable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/what-you-need.rst:48 2f48eff349754dc48f72940ef0fded0d
msgid ""
"Developers creating UAV vision applications should consider using a "
"separate Companion Computer, or a Linux based autopilot board."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/what-you-need.rst:52 90c3dc59fb124abe856821a8b3ef9db0
msgid "GPS module"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/what-you-need.rst:54 9fd917d9f10f42ef9fc31068607cf6a3
msgid ""
"Your Copter will *require* a GPS module. The recommended module is "
":ref:`3DR UBlox GPS + Compass Module <common-installing-3dr-ublox-gps-"
"compass-module>` which also includes an a compass. You can check out "
":ref:`other GPS solutions here <common-positioning-landing-page>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/what-you-need.rst:61 bd10af672e4f4776a8187519e9b15a1d
msgid "LiPo batteries and charger"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/what-you-need.rst:66 ec4d300c706f44a6871a16fdcfd892f1
msgid ""
"Copter requires a rechargeable lithium polymer (LiPo) battery. A good "
"rule of thumb is to use 1,000 mAH (milliamp hours) per motor. For a Quad "
"copter, a `4000 mAH LiPo like this one <https://hobbyking.com/en_us"
"/turnigy-4000mah-3s-20c-lipo-pack.html?___store=en_us>`__ would work "
"well. While your copter can use only one battery at a time, we recommend "
"having at least two batteries in stock; more batteries means more flight "
"time. You'll also need a `charging station for your batteries such as "
"this one <https://hobbyking.com/en_us/turnigy-2s-3s-balance-charger-"
"direct-110-240v-input.html?___store=en_us>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/what-you-need.rst:73 554417719aee415ebd5b0a616d6f1198
msgid "Ground Control Station"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/what-you-need.rst:75 ed3797c541ae4b07a714a547e2c57bfd
msgid ""
"The (free and open source) :ref:`Mission Planner <planner:home>` is "
"required if you're going to be loading new versions of Copter onto the "
"autopilot, and for first-flight tuning and calibration. It runs on a PC "
"and can also be used for planning missions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/what-you-need.rst:83 ad2b35765620454fa962d231c84e7e88
msgid ""
"Once your Copter is configured, you may find it more convenient to choose"
" a different ground station - running on the tablet, phone or computer of"
" your choice. The main options are discussed in the topic :ref:`Choosing "
"a Ground Station <common-choosing-a-ground-station>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/what-you-need.rst:89 78c81313476e42cdacae18d98d8ee4ed
msgid "Telemetry Radio"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/what-you-need.rst:91 6e7a4dfde28f4cf596c2426f5870189b
msgid ""
"A telemetry radio allows your Copter to communicate with your ground "
"station from the air using the MAVLink protocol. This allows you to "
"interact with your missions in real time and receive streaming data from "
"your copter's cameras and other components. This adds considerable "
"convenience to your missions!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/what-you-need.rst:97 17bb27aebfdc4ce6b20f2ed2bd02dc81
msgid ""
"We recommend the telemetry radio solutions linked from the "
":ref:`Telemetry Landing Page <common-telemetry-landingpage>`. Remember "
"that if using the :ref:`SIK Radio <common-sik-telemetry-radio>` you will "
"need the version at the permitted frequency for your country - 915 MHz "
"(Americas) and 433 MHz (Europe)."
msgstr ""

